own.harness `pi` harness (packages/own-harness/src/pi/)

The pi harness ports text and code from the Pi coding agent:

  earendil-works/pi (https://github.com/earendil-works/pi)
  Copyright (c) 2025 Mario Zechner
  Licensed under the MIT License; the license text is in LICENSE next to this file.

Ported at commit dd30101cfc5b0609411dd80b6f93adbc14db14cf (v1.5.1; first ported at 3daa20280, v1.2.0-22, refreshed
on 2026-10-30 at e7a0df27c, v1.4.0-211, with the shell fixes of Pi 1.4.0, and on 2026-11-10 at v1.5.1 with the
tightened system prompt, the edit tool's line-ending fix, pi-schema's argument texts, the bash timeout after the
shell exited and the streamed read). The files read are listed with their SHA-256 (LF line endings) in source.json.
The system prompt, tool descriptions, parameter schemas, result and error texts, truncation rules, edit matching and
diff rendering, shell resolution and the ported tests come from those files; they are marked "Ported from
earendil-works/pi" in src/pi/ and test/unit/pi/.

The argument check (src/pi/args.ts) follows the messages and conversion rules of Pi's @earendil-works/pi-schema
(packages/schema, MIT, Earendil Works), whose conversion rules port TypeBox 1.3.27's Value.Convert (MIT,
Copyright (c) 2017-2026 Haydn Paterson). own reimplements the few rules Pi's four tools need and depends on neither.
